## 1. Thresholds and Commercial License

You may use OXR and its Derivative Works without a separate commercial
license, including for internal use and to Provide products or services to
Third Parties, whether free or paid, unless either of the following applies
to you and your Affiliates, on a consolidated basis:

(a) Total Funding exceeds USD 2,000,000; or
(b) Annual Revenue exceeds USD 2,000,000.

If either of the above applies, you must obtain a separate written commercial
license from Licensor before commencing or continuing any use of OXR or its
Derivative Works, whether internal use or Providing products or services to
Third Parties, and whether free or paid.

Personal use and non-commercial research, including academic research,
benchmarking, evaluation, and teaching, are exempt from this Section.

## 2. Attribution

If you use OXR or its Derivative Works to Provide products or services to
Third Parties without a separate commercial license under Section 1, you must
prominently display "Powered by SoMark OXR", linked to
https://github.com/SoMarkAI/OXR , in the user interface of the relevant
product or service. If the product or service has no user interface, you must
display this statement and link in its publicly accessible documentation,
about page, or API documentation, or, if none of these exists, in the
deliverables or service agreement provided to the Third Party. Where a
hyperlink cannot be used, you must display the full URL.

## 3. Termination

Your rights under this License terminate automatically, without notice from
Licensor, if you fail to obtain a commercial license as required by Section 1
or fail to comply with Section 2.

## 4. Definitions and Scope

"Affiliates" are entities that directly or indirectly control you, are
controlled by you, or share common control with you. "Control" means the
power to direct an entity's management or operations through ownership,
voting rights, contractual rights, or other means.

"Provide to Third Parties" (and "Providing to Third Parties") means making
available to any person or entity other than you and your Affiliates
("Third Parties") any product or service that incorporates or uses OXR, its
Derivative Works, or any functionality based on them, by any means, whether
online or offline, including (i) hosted or remote access, such as SaaS, API,
or web services; (ii) distribution of copies, such as software, SDKs,
applications, or devices, or deployment on a customer's own servers; and
(iii) performing services for Third Parties using OXR or its Derivative
Works, including document parsing, data processing, data labeling,
outsourcing, or consulting services, or delivering outputs or results
generated by OXR, whether or not any product is delivered. Use solely by you
and your Affiliates, including by employees and contractors acting on your
behalf, is internal use and is not Providing to Third Parties.

"Total Funding" means the total equity or debt funding raised from any
source by you and your Affiliates, on a consolidated basis, excluding
intra-group transactions to avoid double counting.

"Annual Revenue" means the gross revenue of you and your Affiliates for the
most recently completed fiscal year, on a consolidated basis, excluding
intra-group transactions to avoid double counting. Amounts in other
currencies are measured at their US dollar equivalent.

"Derivative Works" has the meaning given in Apache License 2.0. When
redistributing OXR or its Derivative Works, you must include these additional
terms together with Apache License 2.0. Third-party components separately
